The project is written in Odin language, docs for the language - https://odin-lang.org/docs/overview/, docs for the packages - https://pkg.odin-lang.org/, location of odin.exe compiler and the base/core/vendor inbuilt libraries - D:\dev\odin\toolchain\odin-windows-amd64-dev-2025-11\

It is a project that works as an LSP (Language Server Protocol) for SAP ABAP language (documentation for ABAP language - https://help.sap.com/doc/abapdocu_latest_index_htm/latest/en-US/ABENABAP.html)

Source code lives in "src" folder, tests in "tests" folder.

## Layers and dependency rules (src)

Lower layers must not import higher layers. Allowed import direction:

- **jsonrpc** → core only (no `lang`, no `cache`, no `lsp`).
- **lang/lexer** → core only.
- **lang/ast** → **lang/lexer** only (parser and symbols both consume AST).
- **lang/parser** → **lang/lexer**, **lang/ast** (must not import **lang/symbols**; parsing is syntax-only).
- **lang/symbols** → **lang/ast**, **lang/lexer** (must not import **lang/parser**; resolution consumes AST produced elsewhere).
- **cache** → **lang/ast**, **lang/parser**, **lang/symbols** (orchestrates parse + analysis for documents/workspaces).
- **lsp** → **jsonrpc**, **cache**, and as needed **lang/ast**, **lang/lexer**, **lang/symbols** for features that inspect trees or tables.
- **abap-lsp** (main) → **lsp**, **jsonrpc**, plus OS/runtime.

### Package map (ABAP + IDE)

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|------|------|----------------|
| Lexer | src\lang\lexer | Tokenization, text ranges. |
| AST | src\lang\ast | Node types, `Any_*` unions, `lookup.odin`, `utils.odin`. |
| Parser | src\lang\parser | Builds `^ast.File` from tokens (split across `parser.odin` and helpers). |
| Symbols | src\lang\symbols | `symbols.odin`, `resolver.odin`, `types.odin`, `validate.odin`. |
| Cache | src\cache | Document/workspace state, refresh pipelines. |
| LSP | src\lsp | Protocol handlers (hover, completion, diagnostics, semantic tokens, …). |
| JSON-RPC | src\jsonrpc | Transport/message wrapper. |

## AST nodes: naming and unions

To add a new AST node:

- **Expressions**: name ends with `*_Expr`; struct embeds `using node: Expr,`; add pointer type to **Any_Node** and **Any_Expr** in `src\lang\ast\ast.odin`.
- **Statements**: name ends with `*_Stmt`; struct embeds `using node: Stmt,`; add to **Any_Node** and **Any_Stmt**.
- **Declarations**: name ends with `*_Decl`; struct embeds `using node: Decl,`; **Decl** embeds **Stmt**, so add the pointer type to **Any_Node** and **Any_Stmt** in `ast.odin` (there is no separate `Any_Decl` union).

## After adding or changing an AST node (checklist)

Any change to unions or shapes under `src\lang\ast\ast.odin` (including new pointer cases on **Any_Node** / **Any_Expr** / **Any_Stmt**, or new fields on existing nodes) must be propagated deliberately:

- **Always**: `find_node_at_offset` in `src\lang\ast\lookup.odin` (navigation / “node at cursor” must visit new shapes or children).
- **Symbols**: `src\lang\symbols\resolver.odin` when binding, scoping, or include behavior touches the construct; `src\lang\symbols\symbols.odin` for new **SymbolKind** or table entries; `src\lang\symbols\types.odin` if type inference interacts with it; `src\lang\symbols\validate.odin` if semantic validation walks that statement/declaration/expression.
- **LSP** (as appropriate to the feature): `src\lsp\hover.odin`, `src\lsp\semantic_tokens.odin`, `src\lsp\completion.odin`, `src\lsp\diagnostics.odin`—any file that `#partial switch`es on `derived_stmt`, `derived_expr`, or declaration variants may need new cases or behavior updates.

**Tests**: parser changes → `tests\parser\` (new or extended cases); symbol/resolver or validation changes → `tests\symbols\` (and other suites if a shared behavior regresses).

To build the project, thus checking if there are any compilation errors, run command ".\build.bat debug abap-lsp" or ".\build.bat abap-lsp" (debug is default unless `release` is passed).

Every meaningful change to parsing logic, in src\lang\parser\parser.odin, with additions to parsing patterns should have new tests created under tests\parser directory, split into files whenever there is a big chunk of tests related to some part of the language (such as all declarations, or all OOP-related functionality).

No need to add "stmt.derived_stmt = stmt" or "expr.derived_expr = expr" statements in the parsing logic while constructing the AST nodes, this is already taken care by src\lang\ast\utils.odin's new_from_range or new_from_tokens procedures - with the new procedure provided as a common overload entry point via 
```
new :: proc {
	new_from_range,
	new_from_tokens,
}
```



## Platform
This is Window development platform, if you would like to chain commands do so using ";" (semicolon) instead of "&&" (double ampersand), *.bat scripts should be run prefixed with ".\" (like ".\build.bat" or ".\test.bat").


## Tests
To run tests execute command ".\test.bat" - it runs all the tests and outputs errors if any found, otherwise confirming that all tests were successful.